WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.480
Let's get into first principles daily, episode 46.

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:07.380
Today, one example of first principles thinking in action.

00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:11.380
Raising animals for protein wastes most input energy

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:12.580
on the animal's life.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:16.000
Microbes could brew the same molecules for far less.

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:19.500
Consider what happens when a kilogram of beef protein

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:20.400
reaches the plate.

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:23.960
The animal has already consumed roughly 10 times

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:25.140
its own weight in feed.

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:28.680
Most of that energy goes into movement, metabolism

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:32.140
and maintenance rather than into building the amino acids

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:33.440
that become the protein.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:37.540
In a bioreactor, the same amino acids can be assembled

00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:39.920
directly from sugars and nitrogen salts

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:41.260
by engineered microbes.

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:44.180
Every intermediate organism is skipped.

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:46.100
The difference between those two routes

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:48.040
is not a small efficiency tweak.

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:52.620
It separates a process whose costs are locked in by biologies

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:55.760
overhead from one whose costs come from equipment,

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:58.560
purification and regulatory steps

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:01.660
that have not yet been pushed toward their physical limits.

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:05.420
The atoms themselves stay ordinary commodity inputs

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:06.360
in either case.

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:10.100
Carbon chains, nitrogen groups and sulfur bridges

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:12.220
can arrive through room-infermentation

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:14.500
or through a stainless steel tank.

00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:16.980
Once the animal's lifetime maintenance

00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:19.940
drops out of the equation, the overhead attached

00:01:19.940 --> 00:01:22.020
to each path diverges sharply.

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:25.120
Livestock protein has always been produced

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:27.800
by a supply chain built around whole animals.

00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:30.940
That was the only scalable method available

00:01:30.940 --> 00:01:32.580
for most of human history.

00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:36.320
Farmers, packers and retailers optimized inside

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:38.320
that constraint through selective breeding,

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:42.120
better feed conversion ratios and higher carcass yields.

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:45.340
The fundamental architecture never changed.

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:49.080
An entire organism must still be grown, fed, housed

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:51.440
and slaughtered to harvest a few kilograms

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:52.960
of the desired molecules.

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:56.120
The finished retail price therefore carries

00:01:56.120 --> 00:01:58.640
the full lifetime energy budget of the animal

00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:02.180
plus the capital tied up in land, barns, transport

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:05.240
and processing plants sized for seasonal throughput.

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:09.100
Feed alone makes up the largest share of variable cost.

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:11.880
A steer may require eight to 10 kilograms

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:15.080
of dry matter per kilogram of live weight gain.

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:17.600
Only a fraction of that dry matter

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:19.020
becomes edible protein.

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:23.060
Maneer handling, veterinary care and mortality losses

00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:24.780
add further layers on top.

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:27.760
Slotter houses and fabrication plants

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:31.660
are capital intensive facilities that run on fixed schedules,

00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:35.560
carrying costs for inventory and cold storage build up

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:37.100
whenever throughput falls.

00:02:37.820 --> 00:02:39.820
Regulatory and permitting timelines

00:02:39.820 --> 00:02:42.280
for new facilities stretch into years.

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:44.780
That discourages rapid iteration

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:47.000
and keeps the industry concentrated

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:49.100
among a handful of large operators.

00:02:49.580 --> 00:02:51.940
Because every participant treats the animal

00:02:51.940 --> 00:02:54.240
as the indivisible unit of production,

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:57.420
cost reduction efforts stay inside that frame.

00:02:57.940 --> 00:03:00.580
They chase slightly better feed efficiency here

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:03.060
or marginally faster line speeds there.

00:03:03.740 --> 00:03:06.200
The result is an entrenched price structure

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:08.780
that feels inevitable inside the industry.

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:11.120
Yet the protein molecules themselves

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:13.160
are ordinary chains of carbon,

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:15.460
nitrogen, oxygen and hydrogen.

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:18.700
Any organism that can express the right genes

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:19.800
can assemble them.

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:23.660
One common objection is that animals also supply fat,

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:26.420
hide and bone that find secondary markets.

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:30.580
Those co-products still require the same upstream animal

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:32.040
to be raised and processed.

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:35.040
So the marginal cost of the protein fraction

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:37.100
stays tied to the full organism.

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:40.940
Another objection holds that past your based systems

00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:42.880
use land unsuitable for crops.

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:46.700
Even there, the protein yield per hectare stays low

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:49.200
because most photosynthetic energy supports

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:51.620
the animal's respiration and locomotion

00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:53.800
rather than protein deposition.

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:57.800
The same logic runs downstream through rendering plants,

00:03:58.220 --> 00:04:00.640
hide processors and tallow refineries.

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:03.840
Those facilities are sized to carcass volume,

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:06.020
not to the protein molecules alone.

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:08.740
Capital stays locked into equipment

00:04:08.740 --> 00:04:11.920
whose utilization rate is governed by slaughter schedules

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:13.820
rather than by continuous demand

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:16.000
for a single molecular product.

00:04:16.580 --> 00:04:18.860
A rough magic wand estimate starts

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:20.400
with the elemental composition

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:22.220
of a typical dietary protein.

00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:25.660
That composition is about 50% carbon,

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:29.320
25% oxygen, 15% nitrogen,

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:32.040
and smaller fractions of hydrogen and sulfur.

00:04:33.060 --> 00:04:36.660
Commodity glucose or sucrose supplies the carbon skeleton

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:41.640
at roughly 0.30 to 0.50 dollars per kilogram.

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:45.080
ammonia or urea supplies nitrogen

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:47.320
at similar or lower unit cost.

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:50.920
Adding the minor mineral salts and trace cofactors

00:04:50.920 --> 00:04:53.640
brings the raw material value of one kilogram

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:56.000
of finished protein to something on the order

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:59.340
of one to two dollars under current commodity prices.

00:05:00.220 --> 00:05:03.380
That figure is only an order of magnitude floor.

00:05:03.860 --> 00:05:06.140
It ignores energy for bond formation

00:05:06.140 --> 00:05:08.000
and the inevitable yield losses.

00:05:08.360 --> 00:05:11.960
Still, it already sits one to two orders of magnitude

00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:15.600
below the retail price of most animal protein products.

00:05:16.340 --> 00:05:18.480
Dividing the finished price by this floor

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:21.880
produces an idiot index in the range of 10 to 50

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:24.620
for many cuts of meat once retail markups

00:05:24.620 --> 00:05:26.540
and processing margins are included.

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:29.400
The index is not a precise measurement

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:32.400
because exact public figures for every margin layer

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:33.360
are unavailable.

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:36.880
The magnitude is clear because the material inputs

00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:39.940
are traded commodities whose prices are transparent.

00:05:40.600 --> 00:05:42.680
The gap therefore cannot be explained

00:05:42.680 --> 00:05:44.180
by the scarcity of the atoms.

00:05:44.980 --> 00:05:46.980
It is created by everything that happens

00:05:46.980 --> 00:05:50.120
between the feedstock silo and the packaged product.

00:05:50.700 --> 00:05:53.300
Most of that gap resides in four places.

00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:57.200
The bio reactor or fermenter itself must be built,

00:05:57.680 --> 00:05:59.620
sterilized and operated at scale.

00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:03.400
Stainless steel vessels and their associated utilities

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:05.660
represent the largest capital outlay.

00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:08.740
Downstream purification through cell disruption,

00:06:09.240 --> 00:06:11.640
chromatography, filtration and drying

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:14.140
adds both capital and operating expense

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:17.440
that scale with volume but have not yet benefited

00:06:17.440 --> 00:06:20.280
from the same standardization that turned petroleum

00:06:20.280 --> 00:06:24.020
refining into a continuous low unit cost operation.

00:06:24.800 --> 00:06:27.140
The sugar feedstock, while cheap in bulk,

00:06:27.140 --> 00:06:30.120
still carries agricultural and logistics costs

00:06:30.120 --> 00:06:32.880
that could be lowered by switching to cellulosic

00:06:32.880 --> 00:06:34.140
or waste streams.

00:06:34.880 --> 00:06:38.480
Regulatory approval, labeling rules and facility permitting

00:06:38.480 --> 00:06:41.500
impose multi-year delays whose financing costs

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:44.440
are amortized across every kilogram produced.

00:06:45.180 --> 00:06:47.760
Each of these layers is addressable in principle.

00:06:48.440 --> 00:06:51.540
None is dictated by the chemistry of the protein itself.

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:54.900
Bond formation energy and separation work

00:06:54.900 --> 00:06:57.680
are thermodynamic realities that no redesign

00:06:57.680 --> 00:06:58.520
can eliminate.

00:06:59.280 --> 00:07:02.360
The magic wand floor already excludes those costs.

00:07:03.080 --> 00:07:06.640
The relevant comparison is therefore not zero energy synthesis

00:07:06.640 --> 00:07:10.400
but the much larger overhead of maintaining an entire animal

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:12.580
whose metabolic rate runs continuously

00:07:12.580 --> 00:07:15.580
whether or not it is depositing the target protein.

00:07:16.360 --> 00:07:18.180
Once that overhead is stripped away,

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:20.820
the remaining capital and purification costs

00:07:20.820 --> 00:07:23.980
become visible targets rather than invisible background.

00:07:24.820 --> 00:07:27.580
A redesign would begin with the fermentation vessel.

00:07:28.120 --> 00:07:31.940
Moving from batch to continuous or semi-continuous operation

00:07:32.460 --> 00:07:35.840
reduces the fraction of time spent on cleaning and turnaround.

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:39.580
That directly attacks the capital cost per kilogram.

00:07:40.300 --> 00:07:43.560
Larger vessel diameters and improved mixing geometries

00:07:43.560 --> 00:07:46.680
can further lower the surface area to volume ratio

00:07:46.680 --> 00:07:48.820
that drives sterilization energy.

00:07:49.420 --> 00:07:51.980
Strain engineering that raises product tighter

00:07:51.980 --> 00:07:55.700
and volumetric productivity shrinks the required reactor volume

00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:57.340
for a given annual output.

00:07:58.120 --> 00:08:02.040
Each doubling of tighter roughly has the capital tied up in steel.

00:08:02.800 --> 00:08:07.180
On the feedstock side, substituting lignosalulosic hydrolycides

00:08:07.180 --> 00:08:09.920
or industrial side streams for refined glucose

00:08:09.920 --> 00:08:12.100
removes the agricultural premium

00:08:12.100 --> 00:08:14.480
that currently sits inside the sugar price.

00:08:15.320 --> 00:08:18.340
Downstream replacing packed bed chromatography

00:08:18.340 --> 00:08:21.300
with continuous membrane or precipitation steps

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:24.040
can cut both solvent use and cycle time.

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:28.740
Regulatory costs fall when agencies develop predictable pathways

00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:31.240
for well characterized microbial hosts

00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:33.900
and when facilities are designed from the outset

00:08:33.900 --> 00:08:36.400
around modular relocatable skids

00:08:36.400 --> 00:08:38.880
rather than bespoke concrete construction.

00:08:39.680 --> 00:08:41.340
The hard constraints are real.

00:08:42.040 --> 00:08:44.160
Achieving food grade purity at scale

00:08:44.160 --> 00:08:47.700
still requires validated removal of host cell proteins

00:08:47.700 --> 00:08:49.100
and nucleic acids.

00:08:49.940 --> 00:08:52.520
Texture and flavor remain sensory properties

00:08:52.520 --> 00:08:55.120
that purification alone does not guarantee.

00:08:55.920 --> 00:08:58.900
Consumer acceptance hinges on labeling transparency

00:08:58.900 --> 00:09:02.120
and demonstrated safety data that cannot be shortcut.

00:09:02.880 --> 00:09:05.160
Yet each of these obstacles is narrower

00:09:05.160 --> 00:09:07.660
than the blanket thermodynamic overhead

00:09:07.660 --> 00:09:09.480
of growing an entire animal.

00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:12.500
Each has engineering or policy levers

00:09:12.500 --> 00:09:14.320
that can be pulled independently.

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:18.020
One objection is that continuous fermentation risks

00:09:18.020 --> 00:09:20.460
contamination at food grade standards.

00:09:21.180 --> 00:09:23.760
Pharmaceutical monoclonal antibody plants

00:09:23.760 --> 00:09:25.860
already run continuous perfusion

00:09:25.860 --> 00:09:27.820
at far higher purity requirements.

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:31.520
That suggests the barrier is one of validated design

00:09:31.520 --> 00:09:33.860
rather than fundamental impossibility.

00:09:34.600 --> 00:09:37.200
Another objection concerns flavor precursors

00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:39.420
that develop only during animal aging.

00:09:40.140 --> 00:09:41.760
Those can be added post fermentation

00:09:42.340 --> 00:09:44.720
or produced by additional enzymatic steps

00:09:44.720 --> 00:09:48.020
once the core protein stream is decoupled from the animal.

00:09:48.880 --> 00:09:51.000
When the dominant costs sits in the vessel

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:53.920
and the validation paperwork rather than in the atoms,

00:09:54.340 --> 00:09:57.040
the next decisive move is to redesign the vessel

00:09:57.040 --> 00:09:59.040
and the validation process together

00:09:59.040 --> 00:10:00.640
so they reinforce each other.

00:10:01.420 --> 00:10:03.520
When feedstock and purification steps

00:10:03.520 --> 00:10:06.180
are still scaled from pharmaceutical precedents,

00:10:06.620 --> 00:10:09.020
the first signal of progress is a pilot line

00:10:09.020 --> 00:10:11.340
whose unit operations are already sized

00:10:11.340 --> 00:10:13.240
for food grade continuous flow

00:10:13.880 --> 00:10:16.600
rather than adapted from batch drug manufacturing.

00:10:17.240 --> 00:10:20.100
Who will publish the first public mass balance sheet

00:10:20.100 --> 00:10:22.160
that tracks every kilogram of sugar

00:10:22.160 --> 00:10:25.500
into a kilogram of finished protein at pilot scale?

00:10:26.020 --> 00:10:27.400
And what will that sheet reveal

00:10:27.400 --> 00:10:30.040
about which single step still multiplies cost

00:10:30.040 --> 00:10:31.340
by the largest factor?

00:10:32.020 --> 00:10:34.180
That's first principle's daily for today.

00:10:34.680 --> 00:10:36.900
If this changed how you see what things cost,

00:10:37.220 --> 00:10:38.920
share it with someone who depreciated

00:10:38.920 --> 00:10:40.640
and subscribe wherever you listen.

